module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_nominal_value_reaches_a_string_position_and_renders_host_debug_text

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data a_nominal_value_reaches_a_string_position_and_renders_host_debug_text: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_nominal_value_reaches_a_string_position_and_renders_host_debug_text" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "no nominal product or coproduct reaching a String position without a declared conversion, over EVERY crossing: the explicit `as` (v1.compiler.infer validate_cast refusing, located, a nominal source with no declared route, as `true as Int` already refuses, with the Value::Variant | Value::Record arm of v1_interpreter eval_cast's String target unreachable and deleted) AND a builtin String argument such as concat or join (whose formals are untyped in the builtin signature) AND any other untyped crossing; the whole-corpus differential lists the newly refused sites, each fixed forward with its declared conversion" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a nominal product (a record) or coproduct reaches a String position with no declared conversion -- by the explicit `e as String`, or implicitly as an argument of a builtin whose formals are untyped (`concat(\"id=\", e)`, `join`) -- and is ACCEPTED, and at runtime the host's debug rendering of the value is fabricated. HARM: a plausible but wrong string reaches an output or a request (DESIGN section 5, fabricated plausible output); every Int -> record-carrier migration silently turns an existing `as String` over the old Int into this defect, because the cast keeps compiling.",
    "SPECIMEN (found live, gunbc#14732, 2026-10-22): gunbc.superseded_run_starvation_census refresh_pair had `run_id: pair.live_head_run as String`; when the field became the carrier GitHubWorkflowRunId { value: Int } the line kept compiling, a GitHub ListJobs request would have carried `GitHubWorkflowRunId { value: 35447067113 }` as its run id, and its witness stayed green. The declared conversion github_workflow_run_id_wire_text renders `35447067113`.",
    "MEASURED ON MAIN (9cad1c9e6c2, 2026-10-22; one remote dispatch building the `gunbc` binary from v1-compiler and running the probes on the same runner; probes `type P { value: Int }`, `type Q { a: Int, b: String }`, `type C = Red | Green { n: Int }`, `fn main` returning the cast). `p as String` -> compiles, runs, `P { value: 35447067113 }`. `q as String` -> `Q { a: 1, b: x }`. coproduct `Red as String` -> `Red`, `Green { n: 7 } as String` -> `Green { n: 7 }`. `concat(\"id=\", p)` -> `id=P { value: 35447067113 }` (the same rendering without a cast; concat is a second route to the same text). GRAIN: `p as Int` and a coproduct `as Int` are ACCEPTED by the checker and refused at runtime (`TypeError cannot cast P (runtime carrier Record) to Int`), the case the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses owns; `List<Int> as String` is likewise accepted and refused at runtime (`cannot cast List to String`); `Bool as Int` is REFUSED at compile time (`invalid cast: Bool as Int`). So the defect is specific to the String target over a Record or Variant carrier, where the evaluator ACCEPTS rather than refuses.",
    "CHAIN (i), THE EXPLICIT `as` ROUTE (DESIGN section 6b). Link a, the declared-type authority: std.coercion dag_cast_rules rosters only Int, Float and Bool, and a record or coproduct has no route to String declared anywhere. Link b, the checker: v1.compiler.infer validate_cast returns none (admits) whenever either side is outside the dag_cast_rules domain (is_dag_cast_domain_type), so an undeclared crossing is ABSTAINED on, not refused. Link c, the evaluator: v1_interpreter eval_cast, target String, renders `Value::Variant { .. } | Value::Record { .. }` through the host Display (`format!(\"{}\", val)`), commented as 'corpus wire/debug casts for structured values'. EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY: link b. DESIGN section 4 makes coercion the implicit-safe subset of DECLARED conversions and says target realization never decides whether a conversion is legal; validate_cast turns 'no declared route' into 'legal' by abstaining, and eval_cast then supplies a route no declaration owns. Repairing eval_cast alone would leave the checker blessing a cast the evaluator refuses (the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses), so the repair belongs at validate_cast.",
    "CHAIN (ii), THE BUILTIN ROUTE, which never passes through validate_cast. Link a, the declared signature: v1.compiler.method (src/v1/04_method.dag) rosters `concat` as derived_signature(names: [\"a\", \"b\"], method: \"concat\", returns: string_type) -- two NAMED formals with NO declared parameter types, so no declaration says which values a String-returning concat accepts. Link b, the admission: an argument at an untyped builtin formal has no declared type to be judged against (product_value_at_a_scalar_formal_is_accepted, via product_at_scalar_declared_type, judges declared positions only), so a nominal argument is admitted. Link c, the evaluator: v1_interpreter arm \"method_call.concat\" with a Value::Str receiver pushes `format!(\"{}\", arg)` for every argument, and arm \"method_call.join\" renders each element and the separator the same way (`format!(\"{}\", v)`): host Display of a Record or Variant. EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY: link a/b, the untyped builtin formal and the admission that has nothing to judge it by; as in chain (i), the evaluator's Display is a route no declaration owns. Measured: `concat(\"id=\", p)` -> `id=P { value: 35447067113 }`. Confirmed by reading, not yet by a located RED; the join arm is read, not measured.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, home search: the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses owns checker-accepts/evaluator-refuses and names this domain as its RESIDUE, but its harm is a runtime crash; here the evaluator accepts and fabricates. identity_cast_compares_type_spellings and as_cast_has_no_lowered_form (v2 lowering) are different relations. two_admission_authorities_keyed_on_different_relations is the v1/v2 roster fork. annotated_let_judged_by_the_cast_relation_not_the_inhabitance_relation and declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel are declared-type walls, not explicit casts. Filed as its own row because the harm (silent wrong text) and the rung (below the ladder, not a located runtime error) differ from every candidate; it names the_checker_admits_a_cast_the_evaluator_refuses as the sibling that owns the refusing half.",
    "CENSUS, SOUND ONLY AS CANDIDATES: no instrument reads the typed program for this. The seed has no pass listing casts by resolved source type, so the census is a text scan of dag/ and src/v2/ (about 19,000 ` as String` occurrences, 2,400 files, almost all NonEmptyStr or String refinements) filtered by a declared-parameter-type heuristic, then each hit verified by reading. The heuristic misses operands whose type comes from a let, a pattern or a field chain off a binding, and it over-reports bindings shadowed by a pattern; so the list is a LOWER BOUND. The typed census is the Phase 2 whole-corpus differential once validate_cast refuses. VERIFIED WRONG, debug text reaches a produced value: gunbc.source_integration_landing_spine landing_native_refusal `refusal_receipt: refusal.receipt as String` (receipt is a ContentHash coproduct, the text lands in NativeScmRefusal.refusal_receipt). VERIFIED DIAGNOSTIC-ONLY: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_verification_receipt `expected.criteria_digest as String` and `found.criteria_digest as String` (Fnv1a64Structural record, rendered into the VerificationSubjectDiffers expected/found fields of a refusal message). NOT PRODUCTS, ruled out by reading: workspace_microvm_access host_key (NonEmptyStr), nccl NcclChannelUnreadableLines causes (NonEmptyStr), custody and workspace_checkpoint payload bindings (String), the Nat sites (Nat is grounded onto Int).",
    "CHAIN (i) REPAIRED (gunbc#14784), AND THE CLASS HAS NOT CLIMBED. WHAT CHANGED: v1.compiler.infer validate_cast refuses a cast whose source is a nominal product or coproduct with no declared route, as `invalid cast: X as Y: a nominal value has no declared conversion`, abstaining only for a declaration that kernel_grounding_rows carries a row for (Nat) and for the std.types Unit placeholder, both keyed on the exact DeclarationRef read by v1.compiler.infer_env type_reference_declaration_ref (an unrecovered declaration is NOT exempt and refuses, located); v1_interpreter eval_cast's Record/Variant String arm, which rendered host Display, is deleted. EVIDENCE: test.claim.nominal_cast_wall_witness (record and coproduct REDs refused, FAIL on the pre-repair seed; controls Int as String, NonEmptyStr as String, identity, a declared route, n as Int for a Nat, and none as T? accepted); the whole-corpus differential on srv2 (sorted blocking `error[` lines of the full-corpus compile, a seed built from each tree), AFTER fc08c280b62, which carries the declaration-keyed exemptions, against BEFORE ed5930a0cc8, 434 blocking lines in both, 0 newly refused and 0 no longer refused, with the 42 genuine sites fixed forward through their owners' conversions; the v2 reading, where every nominal-to-String probe is refused under ONE rule (NoTargetCandidate) and GroundingNotDerived is UNMEASURED because probe sources take no imports. RUNG at the explicit-`as` path's grain: structurally guaranteed on the seed path for a source whose type reference resolves to a declaration; the wall does not read the reference-location fallback (rung_drop type_reference_location_fallback_keys_production_realization) for its exemptions, though type_reference_declaration_ref itself has fallbacks (resolved node, env binding, name lookup) that this PR did not audit, and a nominal value whose type never reaches the cast site as a Resolved node still abstains in validate_cast (unresolvable source). THE CLASS: the row's rung field is UNCHANGED, because its every-crossing trigger is unmet. CHAIN (ii) STILL FABRICATES: builtin String arguments with untyped formals (concat, join) reach no cast check; the locus is derived_signature in src/v1/04_method.dag, and the measured specimen is `concat(\"id=\", p)` with p a record, which compiles and renders the host debug text. That route is its own change.",
    "CHAIN (ii) REPAIRED ON THE SEED, ARM (a) (lane decision by warm-crane-219, 2026-10-24), AND THE CLASS STILL DOES NOT CLIMB. FORK CENSUS (DESIGN section 6b): one rule -- a value reaching a kernel host-text position was admitted by its text representation alone, never by whether its declaration has a route into text -- with three leaves: validate_cast at `as` (chain (i)), v1.compiler.infer builtin_text_argument_crossing_diags at every formal v1.compiler.method builtin_host_text_param_names declares (its NotText arm returned nothing), and the algebra-method route a bare `concat(\"id=\", p)` and every `join` actually take (no judgment at all). WHAT CHANGED: v1.compiler.infer value_type_is_declared_nominal is the ONE predicate (declared product or coproduct; exempt, exactly as chain (i) exempted: kernel_grounding_rows carriers, std.types Unit and the solver Unit placeholder, keyed on identity; std.types Bool is the coproduct True | False and refuses at `as` on main, so it refuses at the host-text formals too, with reason text that calls it nominal until a kernel-scalar arm of the judgment gives it its own; the kernel Optional, Map, RestResult, Hash and Callable mints are not exempt); cast_source_is_declared_nominal is deleted and validate_cast consumes the predicate; builtin_text_argument_crossing_diags consults it on the NotText and TextRepresentationUnidentified arms; algebra_method_host_text_crossing_diags consults it at NamedTemplate String formals, at ReceiverSelf formals when the template returns ReceiverSelf and the call's result is host text, and at each receiver element when v1.compiler.method template_renders_receiver_elements_as_host_text (std.algebra collection_join_shape, keyed on the template, not the spelling). Refusal: `nominal X at host text <position>: no declared conversion`. EVIDENCE: test.claim.nominal_host_text_argument_wall_witness (REDs: record, unit-arm and record-arm coproduct, an imported coproduct (extdeps.languages.json.parse JsonDocumentGap), a kernel Optional (Int?) and a kernel Bool at concat; String? and Bool elements at join; record and coproduct elements at join; record and coproduct separator at join; record at string_length, which climbs the rest of the registry's host-text formals from a runtime TypeError to a compile refusal; controls String, NonEmptyStr, extdeps.languages.json.parse json_document_gap_text, kernel Int and Nat, and a local parameter spelled join); test.claim.nominal_cast_wall_witness gains a Bool RED (`b as String`, refused as on main). NOT CONSTRUCTED: a nominal the text judge reads as TextRepresentationUnidentified. A record or coproduct declaration reads NotText (it is no alias), so Unidentified needs an unreadable declaration binding or an alias cycle, which no accepted probe source produced; the predicate is consulted on that arm regardless. FIXED FORWARD (2 sites, the v12 census): extdeps.realization.artifact_store_fs artifact_fs_path wrote a ContentHash into a filesystem path, now std.content_hash serialize_content_hash (every store root is a /tmp/gunbc_* scratch root under std.artifact_store_scratch_grant, so the old path shape is a cache miss, no durable data); gunbc.ci.ci_runner_placement rendered an IntegerOverflow into a refusal reason, now std.checked_arithmetic integer_overflow_text (minted in the owning module). KERNEL SCALARS: Int and Nat stay accepted at concat and join, following the cast's admission (Int, Float and Nat are admitted at `as` on main); the census at concat/join counted Nat 3 (gunbc.merge_admission, content_hash_atom preimages, a keys/hashing concern), Int 0, Bool 0, the measured population of a kernel refusal joining this judgment. DECLARED RESIDUALS, so the class does not climb on these paths (v14 census, warm-crane-219, whole corpus vs b96b5b6a406): an argument whose text representation the judge cannot identify is admitted with its counted advisory (86 at concat/join, mostly branded NonEmptyStr refinements reached through a declaration reference; trigger: the judge identifies branded refinements through declaration references); type-variable positions 33 and unresolved argument types 6 are unjudged (trigger: the crossing judges the solved, substituted type). OPTIONAL LAYER: an optional value (`T?` or the Optional carrier written out) at a host-text position refuses as `optional T? at host text <position>: no declared conversion`, through v1.compiler.infer value_type_carries_optional_layer, the read optional_cast_diags now shares; its last-segment `Optional` test is that read's existing spelling key, so a foreign type spelled Optional over-refuses (a fail-closed spelling-keyed residual). BOOL: std.types bool_text is the one declared Bool-to-text route (ruling: kernel to_string over Bool is the host's Display spelling, no route); v1.dag_collect_support literal_value_fingerprint and the three local bool_text copies route through it, bytes `true`/`false` unchanged. DECLARED RESIDUAL, to_string: its `value` formal is a host-Display rendering position whose nominal and optional judgment is deferred (v1.compiler.method host_display_deferred_formals; the code-point-sequence refusal there is unchanged). Population at 4c09c5ffdfc, whole corpus on srv2 vs a3b8d7dff01 (warm-crane-219): 102 sites, records and coproducts 74 over about 38 types (PreOsRefusal 19, PosixOwnerSpec 6, Fci1AllocationSlotObservation 6, ...) and Bool 28, including records rendered into receipt files and content_hash_of_value preimages of OfferKey and observation identities, so their bytes are durable or identity material. Trigger: the to_string census dispositions every non-text to_string site; the row is then deleted and the wall covers to_string. DECLARED RESIDUAL, a List value as a join element: still admitted and rendered in the host debug form; a List is not a declared nominal, so it is outside this predicate. REGISTRY ReceiverSelf FORMALS: skipped only when some ReceiverSelf argument is unestablished (its inferred type is not Resolved, or it reads as a type variable), and otherwise every one is judged, so two records at concat refuse (witness two_records_at_concat_are_refused); an unestablished Self is unjudged and counted under the unresolved residual (the List concats through an unsolved fold accumulator in src/v2/std/decl_facts_skeleton). DECLARED FRONTIER: the kernel-scalar arm (Int, Nat, Float into text, gunbc#15033 at `as`) does NOT reach the host-text formals in this change; trigger: the typed census of to_string sites by argument type shows zero sites in classes A through E (kernel Int; kernel Nat; Int refinements such as HttpStatus and Port; Nat refinements and measures; machine-width integers) after their sweep to the declared conversions (to_string's `value` is a host-text formal of the registry, so the fold before that sweep refuses every to_string over an Int). RUNG: the minimum across in-scope paths; the v2 native route is UNMEASURED for concat/join, so the class's rung field is UNCHANGED.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
